Description: Build components/imageproc at opt-level 1, for reproducibility
 zola has not been reproducible since 0.23.5 brought in fast_image_resize.
 Two builds of identical source produce binaries that differ by a few hundred
 bytes, always register allocation inside the same handful of functions.
 .
 The cause is in LLVM, not in zola and not in the crate. rustc emits
 byte-identical IR across runs; `opt` then turns that identical IR into
 different output. Bisecting `default<O2>` with -print-pipeline-passes puts the
 boundary at the CGSCC stage, cgscc(devirt<4>(inline,...)): stages 1..15 are
 stable, adding stage 16 is not, and running stage 16 alone on a module proven
 stable gives a different result every time. No individual pass inside it
 varies on its own, which is why this reads as a walk-order problem rather than
 a broken pass.
 .
 The stage enters the pipeline at -O2, so opt-level 1 is the highest setting
 that avoids it. opt-level 2 still varies; this is the minimum that works.
 .
 The override targets the CALLER. components/imageproc is the only crate that
 uses fast_image_resize, and the instability is in the crate that instantiates
 its generics, not in the crate that defines them -- fast_image_resize's own
 rlib is byte-identical on every build, so deoptimising it changes nothing.
 Everything else in zola stays at opt-level 3.
 .
 Verified: three full builds from freshly unpacked source, byte-identical.
 Costs about 129 KB and slower image resizing, in a static site generator.
 .
 This is a workaround, not a repair. Drop it when LLVM fixes the underlying
 non-determinism, and confirm with two builds before doing so.
Author: pkg.haus archive <archive@pkg.haus>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-09-15
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -1,3 +1,9 @@
+# See debian/patches/deoptimise-imageproc-for-reproducibility.patch.
+# Not a performance preference: it works around non-determinism in LLVM's CGSCC
+# pass manager, which enters the pipeline at -O2.
+[profile.release.package.imageproc]
+opt-level = 1
+
 [package]
 name = "zola"
 version.workspace = true
